Spec: Android-compatible Agent control client

Purpose:
  Obtain current service authority using platform-key mTLS and mature bounded HTTP.

Owns:
  ./ControlClient.java

References:
  /control-plane/authority/control_server.sdd

Must:
  Use a pinned mature HTTP client with fixed logical TLS name, explicit IPv4 DNS result, no proxy, redirects or automatic connection retries.
  Keep the nonexportable device key in its platform handle; verify owner PKIX, exact profile and server SPKI.
  Limit complete calls to three seconds, eight in-flight calls and sixty-four KiB reply bodies; cancellation and close abort owned calls.
  Bind the control generation to authenticated hello and reject mismatching server epochs or replies received after close.
  Verify returned current snapshot, exact requested scope and signed lease before exposing Agent-only authority; do not expose owner mutation RPC.
  Permit read-only lease.check batches of at most sixty-four already verified snapshots bound to this client identity, clock and epoch.
  After validating a correlated successful response over pinned mTLS, observe its standard HTTP Date as a forward-only time floor; malformed, failed, redirected or closed replies cannot reset clock or signed expiry.
